18/09/95
gpa.c           changed type LONG in reference to G_vars, to type VARTYPE

translog.c      changed definition of j in outll() to a NUMB and 
                the access functions to ATON line 226

function.c      changed :-
                        PUBLIC LONG  G_vars[50];
                to:
                        PUBLIC VARTYPE  G_vars[50];
                and added 
                        #include "arith.h"
                to the include list at top of file.

actions.c       changed all accesses to G_vars and varspace to type VARTYPE
                from type LONG

gpa.c           changed :-
                        extern LONG G_vars[50];
                to:
                        typedef double VARTYPE;
                        extern VARTYPE G_vars[50];

actions.h       moved :-
                        typedef double VARTYPE;
                from line 59 to line 39 i.e. above the line:
                        #ifdef ACTIONS_C
arith.h
                commented out the define "LONGS"                
                changes PUSHS and PUSHN to use 3 parameters
                changed push declaration
arith.c
                changed push definition

control.c
                changed myfree mymalloc mystrdup & myrealloc to perform
                better memory checking under error conditions

control.h       changed definition of MALLOC FREE STRDUP & REALLOC to
                use __LINE__ and __FILE__
19/09/95
                modified CTOS code to match PC code
                in case of error the PC code should be used as the baseline

gpa.c           changed the function CWaitInp() to set CF=NUMITEM
                to try and force an exit in the form.

fldproc.c
                added code to applyformat() so that right justified fields
                greater than the format length are filled with *'s

arith.h
                changed :
                        NTOA(a,b) sprintf(a,"%0.0f",b)
                to :
                        NTOA(a,b) { sprintf(a,"%lf",b); truncate(a); }
                and added declaration for truncate();
                to resolve rounding on string-numbers

arith.h         
                added truncate(); to remove any data after the decimal point
                from a string-number.

actions.c       
                added {}'s around NTOA's in if() statements

CONTROL.C CONFIG.C FORMHAND.C ACTIONC.C PP.C GPA.C
GPAMAIN.C FUNCTION.C ACTIONS.C TRANSLOG.C FLDPROC.C
TABPROC.C CONFIG.H FR.C

                removed all compiler warning message from Klemens version 
                i.e. the DOS version of the code:

tabproc.c       added debug to CTOS version to find problem between MALLOC
                and REALLOC at line 142 in getnumrec() case 1

tabproc.c       changed l+1 (next record number) to call the database 
                module with MESSAGE_un (URI next)

types.h         added MESSAGE_un

pdxdev.c        added support for MESSAGE_un  PARADOX in pdx_control()

20/09/95

arith.h         
                made the divide() operator truncate the result when
                TURNCONDIV (TRUNCate ON DIVide) is defined

gpa.c           changed (1%2) to (i%2) in line 555

actions.c       added G_checkresult to PUSH(0) on to the stack when
                you return from a LOOKUP() with no valid range

dbm.c(CTOS)     changes calculation of the record buffer length to use
                the actual field lengths not the compressed the numbers
                i.e "9999" is len 4 bytes, NOT 2 bytes.

tabproc.c       check if "nr" returned by getnumrec is ZERO and return before
                any memory allocation etc.

tabproc.c       changed redraw of tables on hot key to force the code to
                redraw it's self by making numrec != the number of records
                in tableinput().

